# Competitor SEO — always check and strengthen

Before publishing or shipping SEO/meta changes for guides (especially `/es` LATAM → España/Portugal and RU pillars):

## Do

1. **SERP scan** for the primary queries (country + residencia / nómada / nacionalidad 2 años / year).
2. Note competitor title/description hooks (demonym, «2 años», thresholds, consulado, Schengen ≠ residencia).
3. Ship **stronger** Emigro `seo_title`, `seo_description`, `excerpt`, `quick_answer`, hub metadata, and LLM layers (`llms.txt` / long-tails / `aiDescription`) — beat their hooks with official sources + Emigro evaluator, without inventing law.
4. Keep full user draft body; fact-check only via short overlays (see `full-guides-no-shorten`).

## Do not

- Ship weak meta like «España desde X 2026: residencia XX» when SERP uses demonyms + 2 años + visa names.
- Skip competitor check because «we already have meta».
- Shorten the guide to chase SERP length.

## LATAM ES defaults that beat lawyers/blogs

- Title: demonym + 2026 + hook (`2 años` / `nómada` / Schengen).
- Description ≤~160: Schengen ≠ residencia · ~€2.849 · NL/IPREM · art. 22 · consulado city.
- `quick_answer` / `aiDescription`: same facts + CTA `/es/wizard`.
